{
  "dom_id": "step-q111943",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Factor the expression $9{v}^{5}+6{v}^{4}+{v}^{3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${v}^{3}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${v}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{v}^{5}+6{v}^{4}+{v}^{3} & ={v}^{3}(9{v}^{2}+6v+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression $9{v}^{2}+6v+1$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{3}(9{v}^{2}+6v+1) & = \\\\ {v}^{3}((3v)^{2}+6v+{1}^{2}) & = \\\\ {v}^{3}((3v)^{2}+2\\cdot (3v)+{1}^{2}) & = \\\\ {v}^{3}(3v+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
